## Why This Is Asked

This question probes practical cost-benefit thinking for client-side experimentation, balancing latency, data transfer, and privacy across edge and cloud contexts.

## Key Concepts

- Local-first feature flags and variant mapping
- Delta configuration updates and offline resilience
- Privacy, data minimization, and compliance
- Cost modeling: storage, fetch bandwidth, maintenance, and break-even analysis

## Code Example

```javascript
// Simple config and selection logic
const FLAGS_KEY = 'ab_flags'
function loadFlags(){
  const raw = localStorage.getItem(FLAGS_KEY); return raw ? JSON.parse(raw) : {};
}
function selectVariant(flagName, userHash){
  const flags = loadFlags();
  const flag = flags[flagName];
  if(!flag) return null;
  // deterministic variant from user hash
  const idx = Math.abs(hashCode(userHash + flagName)) % flag.variants.length;
  return flag.variants[idx];
}
function hashCode(s){ let h=0; for(let i=0;i<s.length;i++){ h = (h<<5) - h + s.charCodeAt(i); h |= 0; } return h; }
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you detect and handle stale flags in offline mode?
- What telemetry would you collect to validate uplift without compromising privacy?

## Why This Is Asked
This question tests the ability to translate product goals into a concrete cost model that accounts for on-device constraints, security requirements, and regulatory concerns. It also probes understanding of trade-offs for multi-app isolation, update mechanics, and privacy-by-design principles.

## Key Concepts
- On-device ML model footprints and TEE (Trusted Execution Environment) architecture
- Cross-app isolation with per-app policy overrides
- Telemetry budgeting and data minimization under privacy regulations
- OTA update economics, delta patching, and cryptographic key rotation
- Compliance frameworks (GDPR, CCPA), privacy-by-design, and break-even analysis

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo-break-even calculator
function needsGoNoGo(serverSavingsPerMonth, deviceCostsPerMonth, months) {
  const netSavings = serverSavingsPerMonth - deviceCostsPerMonth;
  const cumulativeSavings = netSavings * months;
  return {
    breakEvenMonths: deviceCostsPerMonth / netSavings,
    go: cumulativeSavings > 0 && months >= 18
  };
}
```

