## Why This Is Asked

This question probes practical on-device crypto trade-offs for privacy-focused apps.

## Key Concepts
- On-device key management
- Key rotation cadence
- AES-256-GCM encryption
- Impact on battery, CPU, memory
- Privacy/compliance costs

## Code Example
```javascript
async function encryptNote(note, key) {
  const enc = new TextEncoder();
  const iv = crypto.getRandomValues(new Uint8Array(12));
  const alg = { name: 'AES-GCM', iv };
  const ciphertext = await crypto.subtle.encrypt(alg, key, enc.encode(note));
  return { iv, ciphertext: new Uint8Array(ciphertext) };
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How to measure encryption energy impact on mobile?
- How to rotate keys without re-encrypting all notes?

## Why This Is Asked
This question probes practical CBA for a local-first search feature, balancing storage, CPU, and privacy.

## Key Concepts
- On-device indexing
- Delta sync costs
- Privacy/compliance
- Update cadence and go/no-go criteria

## Code Example
```javascript
function indexRepo(files) {
  // naive tokenization
  const index = {};
  for (const f of files) {
    const tokens = f.content.split(/\\W+/).filter(Boolean);
    tokens.forEach(t => (index[t] ||= []).push(f.path));
  }
  return index;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you measure user time saved and energy impact to validate the break-even?
- How would you design for monorepos and very large repos with incremental indexing?

## Why This Is Asked

Tests ability to design a cost-benefit for privacy-preserving identity with ZK; evaluates crypto choices, on-device constraints, privacy, compliance, rollout, and measurement plans.

## Key Concepts

- Zero-knowledge proofs (ZK)
- On-device cryptography and secure enclaves
- Energy/perf trade-offs in mobile environments
- Data minimization and regulatory compliance
- Rollout strategy and success metrics

## Code Example

```javascript
// Pseudo API for per-proof cost estimation
function estimateProofCost(securityLevel, proofSizeKB) {
  const cpuPerBit = securityLevel >= 128 ? 2 : 1;
  const energyPerOp = securityLevel >= 128 ? 0.5 : 0.2;
  return { cpuOps: proofSizeKB * 1000 * cpuPerBit, energyJ: proofSizeKB * 0.01 * energyPerOp };
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you validate the security of the ZK protocol chosen?
- How would you handle offline onboarding if network is unavailable?

## Why This Is Asked

Assess the ability to translate usage into a cost-benefit framework for a privacy-preserving, offline-first sync feature, including storage, energy, and cloud costs.

## Key Concepts

- Data sizing and retention policies
- On-device energy and encryption overhead
- Cloud storage/egress pricing and scaling
- Privacy/compliance considerations and opt-in flows
- Go/no-go criteria and break-even analysis

## Code Example

```javascript
function estimateAnnualCost({clipsPerDay, bytesPerClip, retentionDaysCloud, users, costPerGB}) {
  const perUserMB = clipsPerDay * bytesPerClip * 365 / (1024 * 1024);
  const cloudGB = clipsPerDay * bytesPerClip * retentionDaysCloud * 365 / (1024 * 1024 * 1024);
  const monthlyCost = (cloudGB * costPerGB) / 12;
  const totalMonthly = monthlyCost * users;
  return { perUserMB, cloudGB, totalMonthly };
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you adjust the CBA for user growth and volatility in clip frequency?
- What privacy/consent controls would you expose, and how would they impact costs and ROI?

## Why This Is Asked

Tests ability to model a device-resident telemetry system that serves multiple apps while enforcing data minimization and consent, balancing privacy, UX impact, and backend savings.

## Key Concepts

- Data deduplication and cross-app coordination on-device
- Consent lifecycle and policy enforcement across tenants
- On-device aggregation, sampling, and energy budgeting
- Privacy/compliance costs and drift monitoring
- Rollout strategy, break-even analysis, and governance

## Code Example

```javascript
function aggregateDeltas(deltas) {
  // de-duplicate by user/app+event, then sample
  const seen = new Set();
  const out = [];
  for (const d of deltas) {
    const key = d.userId + '|' + d.appId + '|' + d.eventId;
    if (!seen.has(key)) {
      seen.add(key);
      if (Math.random() < d.sampleRate) out.push(d.aggregate);
    }
  }
  return out;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you quantify cross-app dedup cost vs backend savings?
- What would a staged rollout look like to minimize risk and ensure compliance?
